{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b09b9b8c9145f22f","type":"tool_result","content":"kube-rbac-proxy.md\nmlflow-operator.md\nmlflow.md\nPLATFORM.md\n----\n# Component: mlflow\n\n## Metadata\n\n- **Repository**: https://github.com/red-hat-data-services/mlflow.git\n- **Version**: 1cccfac973b98eea1cafe03565da6a47ea08c449\n- **Distribution**: RHOAI\n- **Languages**: Python\n- **Deployment Type**: Python SDK\n- **Generated By**: Claude Opus 4.6 on 2026-08-13\n\n## Purpose\n\n**Short**: MLflow Tracking Server providing experiment tracking, model registry, and artifact serving with Kubernetes-native authentication and workspace isolation for RHOAI. [source: Dockerfile.konflux:80, mlflow/server/__init__.py:218-226, mlflow/tracking/request_auth/kubernetes_request_auth_provider.py:1-11]\n\n**Detailed**: MLflow is deployed as a containerized tracking server on port 5000, serving the MLflow UI, REST API, and artifact proxy behind the `kubernetes-auth` authentication plugin from the external `mlflow-kubernetes-plugins` package (v1.5.0). The server runs Python 3.12 under gunicorn/uvicorn on a UBI9-minimal base image, with Kubernetes service account bearer tokens providing authentication and the `mlflow/server/auth` module enforcing RBAC-based authorization with roles, permissions, and per-resource access control. The `--enable-workspaces` flag activates multi-tenant workspace isolation backed by a Kubernetes workspace store (`kubernetes://`), where each workspace maps to a Kubernetes namespace. The component surface includes 6 architecture components—the container entrypoint, gunicorn and uvicorn ASGI/WSGI servers, the mlflow and mlflow-skinny Python services, and the mlflow-tracing SDK—exposing 48 HTTP endpoints for experiment tracking, model registry, gateway proxy, assistant, job execution, and MCP server APIs. External integrations include S3-compatible storage via boto3, Google Cloud Storage, and the Kubernetes API for project execution as Jobs. [source: Dockerfile.konflux:49-58, 76-80, requirements/konflux-pypi.in:13, mlflow/server/__init__.py:218-226, mlflow/server/auth/__init__.py:229-367, mlflow/tracking/request_auth/kubernetes_request_auth_provider.py:203-258, mlflow/projects/kubernetes.py:8-9, 32-49]\n\n## Architectural Analysis\n\nMLflow operates in RHOAI as a multi-tenant experiment tracking and model registry server. The container entrypoint (`Dockerfile.konflux:80`) starts the MLflow tracking server with three key flags that define its RHOAI-specific behavior: `--app-name kubernetes-auth` loads the server-side authentication plugin from the separately packaged `mlflow-kubernetes-plugins` (v1.5.0, installed from PyPI via hermetic Konflux build), `--enable-workspaces` activates namespace-scoped workspace isolation, and `--workspace-store-uri kubernetes://` delegates workspace storage to the Kubernetes API. [source: Dockerfile.konflux:80, requirements/konflux-pypi.in:13]\n\nThe authentication architecture has two layers. On the server side, the `--app-name kubernetes-auth` entry point loads an auth middleware plugin that intercepts API requests. On the client side, `mlflow/tracking/request_auth/kubernetes_request_auth_provider.py` provides two auth providers activated via `MLFLOW_TRACKING_AUTH`: `kubernetes` (bearer token only) and `kubernetes-namespaced` (bearer token plus `X-MLFLOW-WORKSPACE` header derived from the pod's service account namespace). Both resolve credentials from the Kubernetes service account token file at `/var/run/secrets/kubernetes.io/serviceaccount/token`, falling back to kubeconfig when running outside a cluster. The core `mlflow/server/auth/__init__.py` module provides RBAC enforcement with role-based permissions, per-resource access control for experiments, registered models, gateway endpoints, and workspaces. [source: mlflow/tracking/request_auth/kubernetes_request_auth_provider.py:1-11, 38-41, 203-294, mlflow/server/auth/__init__.py:229-367, mlflow/server/__init__.py:218-226]\n\nThe Kubernetes API integration serves two distinct purposes: project execution (creating and monitoring Kubernetes Jobs for ML experiment runs via `mlflow/projects/kubernetes.py`) and workspace management (the `kubernetes://` workspace store URI). The project execution path uses the `kubernetes` Python client to construct Job manifests, push container images, and poll Job status. [source: mlflow/projects/kubernetes.py:8-9, 32-49, Dockerfile.konflux:80]\n\nThe RHOAI container disables several upstream features via environment variables: `MLFLOW_ENABLE_AI_GATEWAY=false`, `MLFLOW_ENABLE_ASSISTANT=false`, `MLFLOW_SERVER_ENABLE_JOB_EXECUTION=false`, and `MLFLOW_DISABLE_TELEMETRY=true`. This means the gateway and assistant HTTP endpoints present in the codebase are not active in the default RHOAI deployment. [source: Dockerfile.konflux:38-43]\n\n## Provenance\n\n### Repo Lineage\n\n| Role | Repository | Sync Mechanism | Sync Branch | Sync Workflows | Detection Method |\n|----|----------|--------------|-----------|--------------|----------------|\n| Upstream | https://github.com/mlflow/mlflow | -- | -- | -- | known_mapping |\n| Midstream | https://github.com/opendatahub-io/mlflow | manual | main | -- | sync_config |\n| Downstream | https://github.com/red-hat-data-services/mlflow | manual | main | `check-operator-workflow-sync.yml`, `version-sync.yml` | local_analysis |\n\n### Aliases\n\n| Current Name | Previous Name | Type | Context |\n|------------|-------------|----|-------|\n\n## Architecture Components\n\n| Component | Type | Purpose |\n|---------|----|-------|\n| Dockerfile.konflux:CMD | Container entrypoint | [\"python3.12\", \"-m\", \"mlflow\", \"server\", \"--host\", \"0.0.0.0\", \"--port\", \"5000\", \"--app-name\", \"kubernetes-auth\", \"--enable-workspaces\", \"--workspace-store-uri\", \"kubernetes://\", \"--serve-artifacts\"] |\n| gunicorn | Python ASGI/WSGI server | Python entrypoint |\n| mlflow | Python Service (FastAPI), Python console script | MLflow is an open source platform for the complete machine learning lifecycle; mlflow.cli:cli |\n| mlflow-skinny | Python Service (FastAPI) | MLflow is an open source platform for the complete machine learning lifecycle |\n| mlflow-tracing | Python SDK | MLflow Tracing SDK is an open-source, lightweight Python package that only includes the minimum set of dependencies and functionality to instrument your code/models/agents with MLflow Tracing. |\n| uvicorn | Python ASGI/WSGI server | Python entrypoint |\n\n## APIs Exposed\n\n### Custom Resource Definitions (CRDs)\n\n| Group | Version | Kind | Scope | API Role | Purpose |\n|-----|-------|----|-----|--------|-------|\n\n### Serving Runtime Definitions\n\n| Name | Kind | API Group | Version | Scope | Supported Model Formats | Container Images | Built-in Adapter | Source |\n|----|----|---------|-------|-----|-----------------------|----------------|----------------|------|\n\n### HTTP Endpoints\n\n| Path | Method | Port | Protocol | Transport | Encryption | Auth | Owner | Purpose |\n|----|------|----|--------|---------|----------|----|-----|-------|\n| / | GET |  | HTTP/HTTPS | Unknown | Configurable | Unknown |  | Python API route |\n| /agent-handler | POST |  | HTTP/HTTPS | Unknown | Configurable | Unknown |  | Python API route |\n| /agent/info | GET |  | HTTP/HTTPS | Unknown | Configurable | Unknown |  | Python API route |\n| /ajax-api/3.0/jobs/ | POST |  | HTTP/HTTPS | Unknown | Configurable | Unknown |  | Python API route |\n| /ajax-api/3.0/jobs/cancel/{job_id} | PATCH |  | HTTP/HTTPS | Unknown | Configurable | Unknown |  | Python API route |\n| /ajax-api/3.0/jobs/search | POST |  | HTTP/HTTPS | Unknown | Configurable | Unknown |  | Python API route |\n| /ajax-api/3.0/jobs/{job_id} | GET |  | HTTP/HTTPS | Unknown | Configurable | Unknown |  | Python API route |\n| /ajax-api/3.0/mlflow/assistant/config | GET |  | HTTP/HTTPS | Unknown | Configurable | Unknown |  | Python API route |\n| /ajax-api/3.0/mlflow/assistant/config | PUT |  | HTTP/HTTPS | Unknown | Configurable | Unknown |  | Python API route |\n| /ajax-api/3.0/mlflow/assistant/message | POST |  | HTTP/HTTPS | Unknown | Configurable | Unknown |  | Python API route |\n| /ajax-api/3.0/mlflow/assistant/providers/{provider}/health | GET |  | HTTP/HTTPS | Unknown | Configurable | Unknown |  | Python API route |","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bdefbd1fc67ed192","agent_id":"aa9fbedecc8803c45","session_id":"acc56831-ee8f-4f4b-89df-cab5630bc453","uuid":"008a913b-54c6-4e52-8a89-8247f3b5ae2d","timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:25:24.048Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b09b9b8c9145f22f","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8009"}
