w (Architecture Review, Build Onboarding, License Validation, etc.) — reflected in human_process_gates signals; not decomposed into epics because components already build and ship (Dockerfile.konflux exists per mlflow.md).\n4. Proposed ACs flagged \"requires PM/Engineering validation\" — carried into epic ACs as written.\n5. Latency target unspecified (OQ1) — handled as measurement AC + conditional caching on E003; if PM/Engineering sets a strict target pre-implementation, caching scope may grow.\n6. mlflow-kubernetes-plugins has no architecture-context file — plugin claims corroborated indirectly via mlflow.md; repo location/access unconfirmed (repo_access=0 on plugin epic).\n\nTiered Delivery: not applicable (no external dependency with uncertain timing — all dependencies internal and existing). Note the intrinsic phasing: P0 server-side capability delivers value with manually-configured deployments; P1 operator topology automates deployment.\n\nComponent Mappings section: MLflow → MLflow (canonical); MLflow Operator → MLflow; mlflow-kubernetes-plugins → MLflow. Note that canonical list has only \"MLflow\".\n\nStaff Engineer Input Overrides section: three items logged.\n\nInvestigation Outcomes section: E001 bounded outcomes (≤3): (A) plugin decoupled + paths resolvable → plugin epic reduces to verification; (B) plugin coupled → refactor within plugin epic; (C) paths insufficient → server approach rewrites (gate_failure_impact). Modeled via gate_failure_impact rather than branch files because the epic set is stable across outcomes — only scope/approach varies. E002 outcome may add tracking-deployment config scope.\n\nNow epic bodies.\n\nE001 body:\n\n# Validate workspace resolution in the artifacts-only server context (title line)\n\n## Description\nInvestigation resolving whether workspace-based validation of artifact requests can function in an MLflow server running in artifacts-only mode, where tracking and model registry stores are not initialized. Produces a 