e store. |\n\nE004-ai-signals.md:\n| change_specificity | 0 | Scope is contingent on the feasibility findings: \"verify and extend\" — the refactor scope (if any) is determined by the investigation outcome, though the target capability is precisely stated. |\n| pattern_precedent | +1 | The plugin already provides experiment-to-workspace mapping for the tracking server's non-artifact operations; the work extends that existing resolution path. |\n| adapter_pattern | +1 | Extends the existing plugin registration pattern (mlflow.workspace_provider entry point group loaded by WorkspaceStoreRegistry) documented in mlflow.md. |\n| existing_foundation | +1 | Existing plugin (v1.5.0, shipped in the MLflow image per mlflow.md); no greenfield component. |\n| open_questions | 0 | The gating unknown (init coupling to tracking stores) is resolved by the blocking feasibility investigation before this epic starts; remaining work is verification/refactor against its findings. |\n| external_dependency | +1 | Internal plugin owned by the MLflow Team; no upstream contribution needed. |\n| human_process_gates | 0 | The refactor is an internal implementation detail pending no specific human approval beyond normal review; strategy-level gates attach to the server and operator changes. |\n| repo_access | 0 | The plugin ships as the external mlflow-kubernetes-plugins PyPI package consumed by the MLflow image; its source repository is not covered by an architecture-context file, so clonability is unconfirmed (tracked as a risk in the epic). |\n| architecture_claims | +1 | mlflow.md corroborates the plugin's role and registration (kubernetes-auth plugin v1.5.0, workspace provider entry point, kubernetes:// workspace store), though the plugin itself has no dedicated context file. |\n\nE005-ai-signals.md:\n| change_specificity | +1 | Target resources (Deployment, Service, HTTPRoute), the exact container command flags, and the reconciliation behavior are specified, with concrete inspection-based