{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a5e401cd313416d","type":"tool_result","content":"5:- **Repository**: https://github.com/red-hat-data-services/mlflow-operator.git\n16:**Detailed**: mlflow-operator is a controller-runtime operator that reconciles three custom resources — `MLflow` (mlflow.opendatahub.io/v1), `MLflowOperator` (components.platform.opendatahub.io/v1alpha1), and `MLflowConfig` (mlflow.kubeflow.org/v1) — to deploy and manage MLflow Tracking Server instances on RHOAI. The MLflow controller renders Helm charts into Kubernetes resources (Deployments, Services, PersistentVolumeClaims, CronJobs, NetworkPolicies) and conditionally creates Gateway API HTTPRoutes, OpenShift ConsoleLinks, and Prometheus ServiceMonitors based on cluster capability discovery. A dedicated NamespaceRBACReconciler watches the platform Auth CRD (`services.platform.opendatahub.io/v1alpha1`) and labeled namespaces to propagate view/edit RoleBindings for workspace-level access control. The operator uses leader election, caches filtered by label selectors, and field-selector-scoped watches for shared RBAC objects to minimize API server load. [source: cmd/main.go:171, 272, 300, internal/controller/mlflow_controller.go:473-552, internal/controller/namespace_rbac_controller.go:48-106, internal/controller/routing.go:46-179]\n22:The **MLflowOperatorReconciler** manages the component-level `MLflowOperator` CRD from `components.platform.opendatahub.io`, acting as the integration surface for the RHOAI platform operator (odh-operator). A dedicated **NamespaceRBACReconciler** watches namespaces labeled with `opendatahub.io/mlflow-workspace`, the platform Auth CRD (`services.platform.opendatahub.io/v1alpha1`), and MLflow CRs to propagate view/edit RoleBindings into workspace namespaces, enabling multi-tenant access isolation delegated through the platform's centralized auth configuration. [source: internal/controller/namespace_rbac_controller.go:48-106, 