{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-b3c063a8-dbf9-4e44-967b-6ea675c4a432","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-85ef31a15615b84e","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8009-tj7h0xkt/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8009-E002.md","content":"# Design artifact traffic routing for the split-server topology\n\n## Description\n\nInvestigation producing the design for how artifact traffic is routed from the main MLflow tracking deployment to a dedicated artifacts-only MLflow instance in the split-server topology. The strategy leaves this as an open question owned by the MLflow Team: it affects the HTTPRoute design and determines whether the tracking server needs a configuration change to delegate artifact operations. The outcome determines the approach and scope of the MLflow operator's split-server deployment work.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Evaluate routing options for getting artifact traffic from the main tracking deployment to the dedicated artifacts-only instance (for example, gateway-level path routing versus tracking-server-side delegation configuration), and select one.\n- Determine explicitly whether the main tracking server requires a configuration change to delegate artifact operations, and if so, what configuration — and whether it is owned by the operator's Helm values (configuration) or requires server-side code changes.\n- Validate the selected design against the operator's existing patterns: Helm-in-operator rendering with Server-Side Apply, and Gateway API HTTPRoute creation conditional on runtime CRD discovery.\n- Record the decision with alternatives considered, impacts on the operator's chart templates, and any impact on the tracking deployment's configuration.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A design document describes how artifact traffic is routed from the main tracking deployment to the dedicated artifacts-only instance, including the HTTPRoute design.\n- The design explicitly states whether the tracking server needs a configuration change to delegate artifact operations, and what that change is if so.\n- The design is validated for compatibility with the operator's existing Helm chart rendering and conditional Gateway API CRD discovery patterns; required chart changes are identified.\n- The decision is recorded with alternatives considered and reviewed by the MLflow Team.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-6 (P1, supporting): determines how the main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance.\n- HLR-5 (P1, supporting): informs the HTTPRoute design for the dedicated artifacts-only instance.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":56276,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bdefbd1fc67ed192","agent_id":"aa9fbedecc8803c45","session_id":"acc56831-ee8f-4f4b-89df-cab5630bc453","uuid":"6b97a58d-c740-4f76-9365-b2f7cb3155d9","timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:32:30.678Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8009"}
