{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-933b7b82-f30e-4800-ac60-0bcccad8db80","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b89bf28b20aef5de","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8009-tj7h0xkt/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8009-E004.md","content":"# Artifacts-only workspace resolution in the mlflow-kubernetes-plugins auth plugin\n\n## Description\n\nMakes the mlflow-kubernetes-plugins auth plugin's workspace resolution function correctly in the MLflow artifacts-only server context, where tracking stores and model registry stores are not initialized. The plugin already provides experiment-to-workspace mapping for the tracking server's non-artifact operations (registered through the `mlflow.workspace_provider` entry point group and loaded by `WorkspaceStoreRegistry`); this epic verifies that resolution in the artifacts-only context and refactors its initialization path if it proves coupled to full tracking server initialization.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Verify the plugin's workspace resolution (experiment-to-workspace mapping via the `kubernetes://` workspace store) in a server context where tracking and model registry stores are not initialized.\n- If the feasibility findings show workspace resolution is coupled to the full tracking server initialization path, factor workspace resolution into an independent initialization path within the plugin, so the artifacts-only server can initialize only the workspace provider it needs.\n- Preserve existing plugin behavior for the full tracking server: no regression to workspace isolation for non-artifact operations (tracking, model registry, prompt registry).\n- Keep the authentication setup unchanged: the kube-rbac-proxy sidecar and `--app-name kubernetes-auth` configuration work identically for the tracking server and the artifacts-only instance. Workspace authorization reuses the existing auth plugin infrastructure; Kubernetes API mechanics (e.g. review API choices) are plugin implementation details, not strategy-level prescriptions.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Plugin workspace resolution returns the correct experiment-to-workspace mapping in an artifacts-only server context with tracking and model registry stores uninitialized.\n- If refactoring was required: workspace resolution initializes via an independent path, and the existing tracking-server workspace isolation behavior is unchanged (regression verified against current non-artifact operations).\n- Existing authentication behavior (kube-rbac-proxy sidecar, `--app-name kubernetes-auth`) is unchanged.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-7 (P1, raised to P0 by priority inheritance): auth plugin workspace resolution functions correctly in the artifacts-only context without tracking store initialization.\n- Enables HLR-2 and HLR-3 (P0) transitively: the tracking server's workspace validation and fail-closed artifact serving build directly on this capability, which is why this epic carries P0 despite the HLR's P1 label.\n\n## Dependencies and Assumptions\n\n- Scope (verification only versus refactor) is determined by the workspace resolution feasibility findings; if the plugin is already decoupled, this epic reduces to verification against those findings.\n- The plugin's source repository is not covered by an architecture-context file; its location and access should be confirmed before scheduling (tracked as a risk in the decomposition summary).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":58250,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bdefbd1fc67ed192","agent_id":"aa9fbedecc8803c45","session_id":"acc56831-ee8f-4f4b-89df-cab5630bc453","uuid":"5c854681-b9f3-4b6f-bdbb-748fb703a785","timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:32:56.517Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8009"}
