{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-30075026-b686-4000-89fd-660e36016bbd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad7be3dc071dadd9","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8009-tj7h0xkt/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8009-E005.md","content":"# Split-server artifacts-only deployment topology in the MLflow operator\n\n## Description\n\nExtends the MLflow operator to deploy a dedicated artifacts-only MLflow instance as a separate Deployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute — a split-server topology — and configures the main tracking deployment to route artifact traffic to that dedicated instance. This is not a single-deployment configuration toggle (Staff Engineer / SME Input): the main tracking server continues to handle experiment tracking, model registry, and prompt registry, while the artifacts-only instance handles artifact serving with workspace validation.\n\n## Scope\n\n- New Helm chart templates for the artifacts-only Deployment, Service, and HTTPRoute, rendered through the operator's existing Helm-in-operator pattern (MLflow CR spec converted to Helm values, rendered via embedded chart templates, applied with Server-Side Apply).\n- Configure the main tracking deployment to route artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance, per the adopted artifact traffic routing design.\n- Propagate workspace configuration (`--enable-workspaces`, `--workspace-store-uri`, `--app-name kubernetes-auth`) to the artifacts-only instance using the same configuration mechanisms the operator already uses for the main tracking deployment.\n- Create Gateway API HTTPRoute resources conditionally based on runtime CRD discovery, consistent with the operator's existing pattern for optional dependencies.\n- Operator validation that rejects configurations where the artifacts-only instance lacks workspace flags — misconfiguration could otherwise let artifact requests bypass workspace validation.\n- Backwards compatibility: MLflow CRs without split-server artifact serving reconcile unchanged (current single-deployment behavior preserved); users configure a single MLflow CR rather than managing individual resources.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given an MLflow CR with split-server artifact serving enabled, when the operator reconciles the CR, then it creates a dedicated artifacts-only Deployment, Service, and HTTPRoute separate from the main tracking Deployment, measured by the presence of distinct Deployment resources with the correct flag combinations.\n- Given the dedicated artifacts-only instance deployed by the operator, the artifacts-only Deployment runs with `--artifacts-only --enable-workspaces --workspace-store-uri kubernetes:// --app-name kubernetes-auth --serve-artifacts`, measured by inspecting the container command in the rendered Deployment spec.\n- The main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance per the adopted routing design.\n- The operator rejects CR configurations that enable the artifacts-only instance without the workspace flags.\n- MLflow CRs without split-server artifact serving reconcile to the current single-deployment topology with no changes.\n- End-to-end verification: workspace-aware artifact serving functions through the operator-deployed split topology, verified against the workspace-aware artifacts-only server build (this coupling is an acceptance gate on this epic's deliverable, not a dependency on the server-side work — chart and reconciler development proceed in parallel).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-5 (P1): operator deploys a dedicated artifacts-only instance as a separate Deployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute.\n- HLR-6 (P1): main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance.\n\n## Dependencies and Assumptions\n\n- The artifact traffic routing approach is determined by the routing design investigation; if that design requires substantive changes to the approach here (or tracking-server-side code changes), this epic's scope is rewritten accordingly.\n- Effort: 2-3 sprints per the strategy's estimate — above the ~2-week epic guideline; the keep-whole rationale and conditional re-split trigger are recorded in the decomposition summary's Health Warnings.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":59000,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bdefbd1fc67ed192","agent_id":"aa9fbedecc8803c45","session_id":"acc56831-ee8f-4f4b-89df-cab5630bc453","uuid":"2454804e-ade3-4e41-9e84-ea034472374b","timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:33:09.470Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8009"}
