{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-90b34ea498103230","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E001\n3\ttitle: Validate workspace resolution in the artifacts-only server context\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n15\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Validate workspace resolution in the artifacts-only server context\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tInvestigation resolving whether workspace-based validation of artifact requests can function in an MLflow server running in artifacts-only mode, where tracking stores and model registry stores are not initialized. The strategy flags this as its principal technical unknown (assumptions marked \"needs validation\", open question owned by the MLflow Team, and the \"auth plugin coupling to full server initialization\" risk). The outcome determines the refactor scope for the mlflow-kubernetes-plugins auth plugin and confirms or redirects the approach for workspace-aware artifact serving in the MLflow tracking server.\n30\t\n31\t## Scope\n32\t\n33\t- Trace the workspace store / auth plugin initialization path in mlflow-kubernetes-plugins and the MLflow server: determine explicitly whether workspace resolution depends on tracking store or model registry store initialization. The strategy's dependency table notes the plugin \"may require extension if workspace resolution is currently coupled to the full tracking server initialization path\", and its risk mitigation directs validating the plugin's initialization dependencies early.\n34\t- Determine whether artifact request paths on the artifacts-only surface (`/api/2.0/mlflow/artifacts/*` endpoints) carry sufficient information (experiment ID or run ID) to resolve workspace membership under the standard S3 artifact layout (`{experiment_id}/{run_id}/artifacts/`), and document limitations for non-standard artifact roots and other storage backends.\n35\t- Security analysis (fail-mode / bypass): determine whether path-based experiment-to-workspace resolution can be bypassed — crafted artifact paths, path traversal, or alternate artifact-serving endpoints — and what validation is required to close any bypass. This satisfies the security investigation obligation for this tenant-isolation strategy; the fail-closed behavior itself is already specified by the strategy (deny, HTTP 503) and needs no investigation.\n36\t- Deliver a written findings report: a go/no-go and approach confirmation for workspace validation in artifacts-only mode, plus a refactor recommendation for the plugin if workspace resolution proves coupled to full server initialization.\n37\t\n38\t## Acceptance Criteria\n39\t\n40\t- The findings report states explicitly, with cited code references, whether the plugin/workspace-store initialization path depends on tracking store or model registry store initialization, and what refactor (if any) is required to decouple it.\n41\t- The findings report states whether artifact request paths carry sufficient identifiers for workspace resolution under the standard S3 artifact layout, with edge cases and non-standard artifact root limitations documented.\n42\t- The findings report documents the bypass analysis for path-based resolution and the countermeasures required.\n43\t- A refactor recommendation (or an explicit no-refactor-needed verification plan) for the plugin is delivered and reviewed by the MLflow Team.\n44\t\n45\t## HLR Traceability\n46\t\n47\t- HLR-2 (P0, supporting): confirms the feasibility and approach of validating artifact requests against workspace membership.\n48\t- HLR-3 (P0, supporting): confirms the approach behind fail-closed workspace validation.\n49\t- HLR-7 (P1, supporting): resolves whether plugin workspace resolution can function without tracking store initialization, determining the plugin work's scope.\n50\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b786fc18ac819a71","agent_id":"ac1ecd5e65bb5f32d","session_id":"acc56831-ee8f-4f4b-89df-cab5630bc453","uuid":"b07c92c9-50b4-40d8-b714-5a0f0ca4ecdd","timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:34:52.232Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-90b34ea498103230","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
