le is accurate —\n122\tmlflow.md's Dockerfile.konflux CMD does run the server with `--app-name\n123\tkubernetes-auth --enable-workspaces --workspace-store-uri kubernetes://\n124\t--serve-artifacts`; E005's is accurate — mlflow-operator.md documents\n125\tHelm-in-operator rendering, Server-Side Apply, conditional Gateway API\n126\tHTTPRoute creation via runtime CRD discovery, and HTTPRoute CRUD in the\n127\toperator's roles; E004's `existing_foundation=+1` and `repo_access=0` match\n128\tmlflow.md (external mlflow-kubernetes-plugins v1.5.0 PyPI package, no\n129\tdedicated context file, repo unconfirmed — carried as Health Warning 6).\n130\tE004's `change_specificity=0` (\"verify and extend\", refactor scope unknown\n131\tuntil the gate) and `open_questions=0` (gating unknown extracted into E001)\n132\tare internally consistent. Two minor calibration notes are recorded (see\n133\tissues list): E001's `source_accessibility=+1` vs E004's `repo_access=0` rests\n134\ton a defensible read-for-analysis (shipped/PyPI package) vs\n135\tclone-for-contribution (repo unconfirmed) distinction that the rationale does\n136\tnot spell out; and E004's `adapter_pattern` rationale attributes the\n137\t`mlflow.workspace_provider`/`WorkspaceStoreRegistry` symbols to mlflow.md when\n138\tthe context file documents the plugin's entry-point loading only generically —\n139\tthe symbols come from the strategy text. Neither contradicts the scored values.\n140\t\n141\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n142\tEvery epic has testable ACs. The strategy's six proposed ACs are carried into\n143\tthe epics (AC 1-4 → E003, including the fail-to-start and\n144\tstores-uninitialized additions; AC 5-6 → E005). E003 adds negative/adversarial\n145\tpath coverage beyond the strategy. E005's end-to-end AC (\"workspace-aware\n146\tartifact serving functions through the operator-deployed split topology,\n147\tverified against the workspace-aware artifacts-only server build\") is correctly\n148\tframed as