{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-94311f41aa1b163c","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E002\n3\ttitle: Design artifact traffic routing for the split-server topology\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n15\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Design artifact traffic routing for the split-server topology\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tInvestigation producing the design for how artifact traffic is routed from the main MLflow tracking deployment to a dedicated artifacts-only MLflow instance in the split-server topology. The strategy leaves this as an open question owned by the MLflow Team: it affects the HTTPRoute design and determines whether the tracking server needs a configuration change to delegate artifact operations. The outcome determines the approach and scope of the MLflow operator's split-server deployment work.\n30\t\n31\t## Scope\n32\t\n33\t- Evaluate routing options for getting artifact traffic from the main tracking deployment to the dedicated artifacts-only instance (for example, gateway-level path routing versus tracking-server-side delegation configuration), and select one.\n34\t- Determine explicitly whether the main tracking server requires a configuration change to delegate artifact operations, and if so, what configuration — and whether it is owned by the operator's Helm values (configuration) or requires server-side code changes.\n35\t- Validate the selected design against the operator's existing patterns: Helm-in-operator rendering with Server-Side Apply, and Gateway API HTTPRoute creation conditional on runtime CRD discovery.\n36\t- Record the decision with alternatives considered, impacts on the operator's chart templates, and any impact on the tracking deployment's configuration.\n37\t\n38\t## Acceptance Criteria\n39\t\n40\t- A design document describes how artifact traffic is routed from the main tracking deployment to the dedicated artifacts-only instance, including the HTTPRoute design.\n41\t- The design explicitly states whether the tracking server needs a configuration change to delegate artifact operations, and what that change is if so.\n42\t- The design is validated for compatibility with the operator's existing Helm chart rendering and conditional Gateway API CRD discovery patterns; required chart changes are identified.\n43\t- The decision is recorded with alternatives considered and reviewed by the MLflow Team.\n44\t\n45\t## HLR Traceability\n46\t\n47\t- HLR-6 (P1, supporting): determines how the main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance.\n48\t- HLR-5 (P1, supporting): informs the HTTPRoute design for the dedicated artifacts-only instance.\n49\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8cd41ae82e822a84","agent_id":"a77de1b6727c54ebd","session_id":"acc56831-ee8f-4f4b-89df-cab5630bc453","uuid":"e318395a-9423-466d-befb-531c02b23f3d","timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:41:16.640Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-94311f41aa1b163c","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8009"}
