{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9b06910d2b7f05dc","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E004\n3\ttitle: Artifacts-only workspace resolution in the mlflow-kubernetes-plugins auth plugin\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8009-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the plugin's workspace resolution is not coupled to tracking\n15\t    store initialization, this epic reduces to verification against the feasibility\n16\t    findings; if it is severely coupled, the refactor scope grows accordingly.\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 0\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n21\t  existing_foundation: 1\n22\t  open_questions: 0\n23\t  external_dependency: 1\n24\t  human_process_gates: 0\n25\t  repo_access: 0\n26\t  architecture_claims: 1\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: High\n30\tai_implementability_score: 5\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\tbranch: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Artifacts-only workspace resolution in the mlflow-kubernetes-plugins auth plugin\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tMakes the mlflow-kubernetes-plugins auth plugin's workspace resolution function correctly in the MLflow artifacts-only server context, where tracking stores and model registry stores are not initialized. The plugin already provides experiment-to-workspace mapping for the tracking server's non-artifact operations (registered through the `mlflow.workspace_provider` entry point group and loaded by `WorkspaceStoreRegistry`); this epic verifies that resolution in the artifacts-only context and refactors its initialization path if it proves coupled to full tracking server initialization.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Verify the plugin's workspace resolution (experiment-to-workspace mapping via the `kubernetes://` workspace store) in a server context where tracking and model registry stores are not initialized.\n43\t- If the feasibility findings show workspace resolution is coupled to the full tracking server initialization path, factor workspace resolution into an independent initialization path within the plugin, so the artifacts-only server can initialize only the workspace provider it needs.\n44\t- Preserve existing plugin behavior for the full tracking server: no regression to workspace isolation for non-artifact operations (tracking, model registry, prompt registry).\n45\t- Keep the authentication setup unchanged: the kube-rbac-proxy sidecar and `--app-name kubernetes-auth` configuration work identically for the tracking server and the artifacts-only instance. Workspace authorization reuses the existing auth plugin infrastructure; Kubernetes API mechanics (e.g. review API choices) are plugin implementation details, not strategy-level prescriptions.\n46\t\n47\t## Acceptance Criteria\n48\t\n49\t- Plugin workspace resolution returns the correct experiment-to-workspace mapping in an artifacts-only server context with tracking and model registry stores uninitialized.\n50\t- If refactoring was required: workspace resolution initializes via an independent path, and the existing tracking-server workspace isolation behavior is unchanged (regression verified against current non-artifact operations).\n51\t- Existing authentication behavior (kube-rbac-proxy sidecar, `--app-name kubernetes-auth`) is unchanged.\n52\t\n53\t## HLR Traceability\n54\t\n55\t- HLR-7 (P1, raised to P0 by priority inheritance): auth plugin workspace resolution functions correctly in the artifacts-only context without tracking store initialization.\n56\t- Enables HLR-2 and HLR-3 (P0) transitively: the tracking server's workspace validation and fail-closed artifact serving build directly on this capability, which is why this epic carries P0 despite the HLR's P1 label.\n57\t\n58\t## Dependencies and Assumptions\n59\t\n60\t- Scope (verification only versus refactor) is determined by the workspace resolution feasibility findings; if the plugin is already decoupled, this epic reduces to verification against those findings.\n61\t- The plugin's source repository is not covered by an architecture-context file; its location and access should be confirmed before scheduling (tracked as a risk in the decomposition summary).\n62\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8cd41ae82e822a84","agent_id":"a77de1b6727c54ebd","session_id":"acc56831-ee8f-4f4b-89df-cab5630bc453","uuid":"d470883d-2437-4cba-a330-e2a052517119","timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:41:19.622Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9b06910d2b7f05dc","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8009"}
