{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8739cc2d4bfaa200","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E005\n3\ttitle: Split-server artifacts-only deployment topology in the MLflow operator\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E002\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8009-E002\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the routing design requires a different topology or tracking-server-side\n15\t    delegation changes, rewrite the chart templates and routing configuration scope\n16\t    accordingly.\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 1\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n21\t  existing_foundation: 1\n22\t  open_questions: 0\n23\t  external_dependency: 1\n24\t  human_process_gates: -1\n25\t  repo_access: 1\n26\t  architecture_claims: 1\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: High\n30\tai_implementability_score: 6\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\tbranch: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Split-server artifacts-only deployment topology in the MLflow operator\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tExtends the MLflow operator to deploy a dedicated artifacts-only MLflow instance as a separate Deployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute — a split-server topology — and configures the main tracking deployment to route artifact traffic to that dedicated instance. This is not a single-deployment configuration toggle (Staff Engineer / SME Input): the main tracking server continues to handle experiment tracking, model registry, and prompt registry, while the artifacts-only instance handles artifact serving with workspace validation.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- New Helm chart templates for the artifacts-only Deployment, Service, and HTTPRoute, rendered through the operator's existing Helm-in-operator pattern (MLflow CR spec converted to Helm values, rendered via embedded chart templates, applied with Server-Side Apply).\n43\t- Configure the main tracking deployment to route artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance, per the adopted artifact traffic routing design.\n44\t- Propagate workspace configuration (`--enable-workspaces`, `--workspace-store-uri`, `--app-name kubernetes-auth`) to the artifacts-only instance using the same configuration mechanisms the operator already uses for the main tracking deployment.\n45\t- Create Gateway API HTTPRoute resources conditionally based on runtime CRD discovery, consistent with the operator's existing pattern for optional dependencies.\n46\t- Operator validation that rejects configurations where the artifacts-only instance lacks workspace flags — misconfiguration could otherwise let artifact requests bypass workspace validation.\n47\t- Backwards compatibility: MLflow CRs without split-server artifact serving reconcile unchanged (current single-deployment behavior preserved); users configure a single MLflow CR rather than managing individual resources.\n48\t\n49\t## Acceptance Criteria\n50\t\n51\t- Given an MLflow CR with split-server artifact serving enabled, when the operator reconciles the CR, then it creates a dedicated artifacts-only Deployment, Service, and HTTPRoute separate from the main tracking Deployment, measured by the presence of distinct Deployment resources with the correct flag combinations.\n52\t- Given the dedicated artifacts-only instance deployed by the operator, the artifacts-only Deployment runs with `--artifacts-only --enable-workspaces --workspace-store-uri kubernetes:// --app-name kubernetes-auth --serve-artifacts`, measured by inspecting the container command in the rendered Deployment spec.\n53\t- The main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance per the adopted routing design.\n54\t- The operator rejects CR configurations that enable the artifacts-only instance without the workspace flags.\n55\t- MLflow CRs without split-server artifact serving reconcile to the current single-deployment topology with no changes.\n56\t- End-to-end verification: workspace-aware artifact serving functions through the operator-deployed split topology, verified against the workspace-aware artifacts-only server build (this coupling is an acceptance gate on this epic's deliverable, not a dependency on the server-side work — chart and reconciler development proceed in parallel).\n57\t\n58\t## HLR Traceability\n59\t\n60\t- HLR-5 (P1): operator deploys a dedicated artifacts-only instance as a separate Deployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute.\n61\t- HLR-6 (P1): main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance.\n62\t\n63\t## Dependencies and Assumptions\n64\t\n65\t- The artifact traffic routing approach is determined by the routing design investigation; if that design requires substantive changes to the approach here (or tracking-server-side code changes), this epic's scope is rewritten accordingly.\n66\t- Effort: 2-3 sprints per the strategy's estimate — above the ~2-week epic guideline; the keep-whole rationale and conditional re-split trigger are recorded in the decomposition summary's Health Warnings.\n67\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8cd41ae82e822a84","agent_id":"a77de1b6727c54ebd","session_id":"acc56831-ee8f-4f4b-89df-cab5630bc453","uuid":"fbbc8177-ab29-4c34-b592-58a79d443ebe","timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:41:20.321Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8739cc2d4bfaa200","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8009"}
